      "topic_id": "congruent_triangle_proof_foundation",
      "prompt": "ABCD is a parallelogram with AB parallel to DC, and AC is one of its diagonals. Which congruence criterion proves that the two triangles are congruent? A) SSS  B) ASA  C) SAS  D) RHS",
      "solution_steps": [
        "angle BAC = angle DCA (alternate angles, AB parallel to DC)",
        "AC is common to both triangles",
        "angle BCA = angle DAC (alternate angles, BC parallel to AD)",
        "These facts match the Angle-Side-Angle (ASA) congruence criterion."
      ],
      "final_answer": "B) ASA",
